# Local deny list: the values of your host.
#
# Copy this file to scripts/host-values.local.deny and put your values into the copy.
# Git ignores the copy. Do not put a real value into this example file.
# scripts/scan.py reads the copy when it exists. A linked worktree uses the
# copy of the main checkout. The report shows the rule number, not the value.
#
# Format: one literal value for each line. The match ignores case and finds
# the value inside longer text. A line that starts with "#" is a comment.
#
# Put these values into the copy:
#   - the name of the machine
#   - each domain that only you use
#   - each user name and account name
#   - the name of a private network, a private project or a private service
#
# Example lines (placeholders):
# my-machine-name
# my-private-domain.example
# my-user-name
